Third-party material
--------------------

The Classic Era quest data in Data/Classic/ is derived from the quest database
of Questie (https://github.com/Questie/Questie), which is distributed under the
GNU General Public License version 3.

Modifications made by Ironship, 30 August 2026:

  * Quest titles and objective text were extracted for Classic Era quest ids
    and rewritten into this addon's own Lua table format.
  * Fields this addon does not use -- quest givers, coordinates, level and
    faction requirements, quest chains, reward tables and objective spawn
    data -- were dropped.
  * No quest text was altered. Where the upstream database has no offer text
    for a quest, this addon has none either and says so rather than inventing
    one.

The extraction is performed by Tools/extract_classic_quests.lua, which is part
of the corresponding source of this work.

The English progress and hand-in lines come from the MultiLanguage addon by
Ruben Zantingh (https://github.com/rubenzantingh/MultiLanguage), used with his
permission given on 2 September 2026.

Blizzard's Game Data API publishes a quest's opening text and objectives and
nothing else. It does not publish the line an NPC speaks while a quest is in
progress, nor the one spoken at hand-in, so this panel could only ever show the
opening text at those two moments and print a caveat admitting it was the wrong
passage.

Modifications made by Ironship, 2 September 2026:

  * 17,138 progress lines and 30,780 hand-in lines were taken, together with
    38,390 objective lines and 18,226 quests the API does not return at all.
  * They were rewritten into this addon's own Lua table format. Fields this
    addon does not use were dropped.
  * No quest text was altered. Where a quest still has no progress or hand-in
    line, the panel says so rather than showing the opening text in its place.

The import is performed by Tools/import_multilanguage.py, which is part of the
corresponding source of this work.

The English quest text for WoW: Forever in Data/Forever/ is put together, field by
field, from four sources (Tools/build_forever_quests.py):

  * What the Forever client itself received from the server, read from its own
    quest cache (Cache/WDB/enUS/questcache.wdb) by Tools/wdb_quests.py.
  * The Classic Era quest data in Data/Classic/, described above.
  * The Forever quest data of the MultiLanguage addon by Ruben Zantingh
    (https://github.com/rubenzantingh/MultiLanguage, revision 87d8e5f, file
    Database/Quests/enUS.lua). The data comes from MultiLanguage and is used with
    its author's permission, which is why his name stands on it here and in the
    README.
  * The quest data of the Spoken addon by Rusty Key
    (https://github.com/rusty-key/spoken-wow, revision 9b2e01c, files
    addons/Spoken_Quests/Data/QuestText.lua and Compendium.lua), released under
    the MIT licence reproduced below.

Some of the Forever quest data in Spoken's files comes from Efficient Games
(https://efficient.games), its EG Link output
(https://github.com/JIVESCORP/eg-link-output-wowf), which is licensed under
CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). It was converted into
this addon's format together with the rest, as the modifications below say. The
text of the quests is Blizzard's in every one of these sources.

Modifications made by Ironship, 12 November 2026:

  * For each quest the fields were chosen from those sources, the game's own
    text first. Spoken's titles, opening texts and hand-in texts were taken only
    where no earlier source has them. Fields this addon does not use were
    dropped.
  * The sources write a player's name, class and race and a line break in
    different ways; they were written one way ({name}, {class}, {race} and a
    newline). Gender alternatives were written as <lad/lass>, as the Blizzard
    API writes them.
  * The MultiLanguage text had the headings of the quest page's reward list
    glued onto the end of some passages ("You will receive:"), and some objective
    fields carried the opening text again; those were removed, and non-breaking
    spaces were made ordinary ones. A few records that are a developer's test text
    were left out.
  * A number the game fills in from its own data tables, which no source has, is
    shown as X.
  * No quest text was otherwise altered or invented. Where no source has a
    passage the panel says so.

